WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:03.122
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:03.255 --> 00:06.076
Let's work through a re-review together.

00:06.467 --> 00:09.611
How do you work through your re-review batch?

00:09.744 --> 00:14.252
Many entities came from SysID, the predecessor database.

00:14.385 --> 00:17.987
Re-review brings them up to date.

00:18.367 --> 00:20.941
Sign in with your Reviewer account.

00:21.074 --> 00:26.044
In the menu bar, open Review, then select Re-Review.

00:26.433 --> 00:31.927
The Re-review table lists
the entities assigned to you, one per row.

00:32.060 --> 00:38.297
Each row ends with four actions: Edit review,
Edit status, Submit entity review,

00:38.430 --> 00:40.753
and a flag to refuse.

00:41.133 --> 00:48.133
Our example is <i>ARHGEF6</i>,
with intellectual disability, X-linked recessive.

00:48.992 --> 00:54.335
Its category is Limited,
and it was last reviewed in 2010.

00:54.700 --> 00:59.623
In the row of <i>ARHGEF6</i>, select Edit review.

00:59.757 --> 01:04.536
A window opens with the current synopsis,
terms and sources.

01:04.900 --> 01:09.830
The Synopsis summarizes the number of patients,
the gene variants,

01:09.963 --> 01:14.827
the severity of intellectual disability,
and further features.

01:14.960 --> 01:19.581
Phenotypes are Human Phenotype Ontology terms found

01:19.714 --> 01:23.333
in at least 20 percent of affected individuals.

01:23.466 --> 01:27.937
For a Limited entity, they are optional.

01:28.300 --> 01:32.307
Variation ontology should
name at least protein truncating

01:32.440 --> 01:36.234
or non-synonymous variation, if your source states it.

01:36.368 --> 01:39.284
Here, only the general term is set.

01:39.417 --> 01:42.157
Publications take PubMed identifiers:

01:42.290 --> 01:46.367
PMID, a colon, and the number.

01:46.733 --> 01:49.826
In Comment, tell the Curator what you checked.

01:49.959 --> 01:52.226
Then select Save Review.

01:52.359 --> 01:54.504
The message says submitted.

01:54.637 --> 01:58.173
For now, your review is only saved.

01:58.533 --> 02:01.059
Now select Edit status.

02:01.193 --> 02:05.839
In Status Category,
choose what the curation criteria support.

02:05.972 --> 02:08.608
A Limited entity can stay Limited,

02:08.742 --> 02:12.628
move to Moderate or Definitive, or become Refuted.

02:12.761 --> 02:17.494
Explain your choice in Comment, then select Save Status.

02:17.867 --> 02:23.010
When review and status are saved,
select Submit entity review.

02:23.143 --> 02:24.688
Check the entity number.

02:24.821 --> 02:27.163
Then select Submit Review.

02:27.296 --> 02:29.946
The entity leaves your list.

02:30.333 --> 02:32.774
Your work passes three stages.

02:32.908 --> 02:35.758
Saved work stays in your list.

02:35.891 --> 02:38.438
Submitted work goes to the Curators.

02:38.571 --> 02:43.214
Only changes a Curator approves appear on the website.

02:43.600 --> 02:46.020
Some entities need a specialist.

02:46.153 --> 02:49.885
In the row of <i>AGTR2</i>, select the flag.

02:50.019 --> 02:51.764
You can add a short reason.

02:51.897 --> 02:55.521
Then select Refuse, needs specialist.

02:55.900 --> 03:00.809
The refused entity leaves
your list and keeps its category.

03:00.942 --> 03:05.979
When your list is empty,
select New batch to ask for more.

03:06.367 --> 03:09.604
Remember: saved is not submitted.

03:09.737 --> 03:13.124
Nothing is public until a Curator approves it.

03:13.257 --> 03:18.926
And refuse an entity that needs
a specialist; it keeps its category.

03:19.300 --> 03:22.748
The full guide is under Review, Instructions.

03:22.882 --> 03:26.827
Thank you for keeping SysNDD up to date.
